criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* Provision of specific informed consent;
* Confirmed or suspected diagnosis of sepsis, defined according to the latest SSC guidelines as: "the presence of a clear or suspected infection with life-threatening organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to infection indicated by a SOFA (Sequential Organ Failure Assessment) score ≥ 2";
* Patients of both sexes, aged 18 years or older;
* Patients evaluated in the Emergency Department for suspected infection requiring hospital admission, at the General Medicine ward of Ospedale Alto Vicentino in Santorso (VI, Italy) or the Emergency Medicine ward of the Policlinico Universitario of Pisa (Italy).

Exclusion Criteria:

* Stay in the Emergency Department of more than six hours, considered as the time between ED admission and ward admission;
* Administration of more than 1000 cc of crystalloid therapy in the three hours prior to patient arrival in the ward;
* Any admission from a facility or ward other than the Emergency Department;
* Sepsis related to an ongoing hospital stay or any sepsis not fitting the definition of community-acquired infection;
* Previous hospital admission within four weeks prior to ED access;
* Sepsis related to trauma;
* Presence of severe oncological disease with life expectancy less than 3 months at enrollment;
* Active major bleeding;
* Dialysis therapy;
* Suspected or confirmed pregnancy;
* Age under 18 years;
* Patients who do not provide informed consent to the study.
